cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Torc-Lite in research, please cite the original TORC paper
  given under preferred-citation. See the repository README for other
  publications describing applications and extensions of TORC.
type: software
title: "Torc-Lite: A Task-Based Parallel Runtime for MPI Applications"
abstract: >-
  Torc-Lite is a lightweight task-based runtime written in C. It combines
  MPI processes and POSIX threads for portable task creation, scheduling,
  synchronization, nested parallelism, and dynamic load balancing on
  multicore systems and distributed-memory clusters.
authors:
  - family-names: Hadjidoukas
    given-names: Panagiotis E.
    affiliation: University of Patras, Greece
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2528-7568
repository-code: https://github.com/CEID-HPCLAB/torc_lite
url: https://github.com/CEID-HPCLAB/torc_lite
keywords:
  - task parallelism
  - MPI
  - POSIX threads
  - nested parallelism
  - distributed computing
  - runtime systems
  - load balancing
  - high-performance computing
